lisa-addressed:
---
[medium] .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml:14 (security)
The release workflow was changed from commit-pinned actions and gooci v0.0.7 to mutable action tags and `go install github.com/compliance-framework/gooci@latest`. This job has `contents: write` and `packages: write` and publishes both GitHub Releases and GHCR images with `GITHUB_TOKEN`, so upstream tag/module movement can change the code that runs with publish credentials and makes releases non-reproducible. The same action-pin regression is present in the test workflow.
Suggested fix: Pin every GitHub Action in the release and test workflows to reviewed full-length commit SHAs, and install `gooci` at a specific reviewed version instead of `@latest`. Use a dependency update workflow to advance those pins intentionally.
Guidance: In .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml and .github/workflows/test.yml, replace all mutable GitHub Action references with reviewed full-length commit SHAs: actions/checkout@v4, actions/setup-go@v5, open-policy-agent/setup-opa@v2, and softprops/action-gh-release@v2. Keep the same action configuration, including persist-credentials: false and OPA version 1.6.0; only change the action refs. In .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml, change `go install github.com/compliance-framework/gooci@latest` to a specific reviewed version, preferably the prior known version `github.com/compliance-framework/gooci@v0.0.7` unless the project owner chooses a newer explicit version. Do not pin `runs-on: ubuntu-latest` as part of this fix unless separately requested; the finding is about executable dependencies and gooci reproducibility.
---
[medium] .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml:31 (correctness)
`release.yml` invokes this workflow for every pushed tag (`tags: ['*']`), but the changed workflow now always uploads the GHCR `:latest` tag. A prerelease or test tag such as `v1.2.0-rc.1` will therefore overwrite `latest`, whereas the previous workflow only promoted non-hyphenated tag names.
Suggested fix: Restore the stable-tag guard on the `latest` upload, for example `if: ${{ startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/') && !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}`, or restrict the release trigger so only stable release tags call the upload step.
Guidance: In .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml, add an `if` condition to the final `gooci upload-single ...:latest` step so it only runs for stable release tag names. The current caller .github/workflows/release.yml triggers on every tag (`*`), so do not rely on the trigger alone unless you also narrow it deliberately. Preferred minimal fix: add `if: ${{ startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/') && !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}` to the latest upload step. Leave the versioned upload to `:${{ github.ref_name }}` unconditional so prerelease/test tags still publish their own tag. Be careful not to put the condition on the GH release upload, gooci install, login, or versioned upload step.

lisa-selfreview: pass 2 (verdict=request_changes)
- [medium] LICENSE:1 (correctness): The branch replaces the repository license text from GNU AGPLv3 to Apache-2.0. That is a substantive relicensing of the whole policy bundle, not a policy implementation change, and there is no accompanying approval or metadata update proving the project has permission to relicense existing code. Pushing this as-is can make downstream use and distribution legally incorrect.
- [low] Makefile:5 (test quality): The changed `validate` target now runs `opa check policies` while README and CI both require `opa check --strict policies`. This makes the local validation command weaker than the documented and enforced check, so contributors can miss strict-mode Rego issues until CI.
